    <ferc:AttestationName id="f-364" contextRef="c-02">T.J. Winczewski</ferc:AttestationName>
    <ferc:AttestationTitle id="f-365" contextRef="c-02">Vice President</ferc:AttestationTitle>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-367" contextRef="c-02">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: 1em; text-align: inherit"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Seaway Crude Pipeline Company LLC (&amp;quot;Seaway&amp;quot;), a Delaware limited liability company, was formed in March 2012. Seaway is wholly owned by Seaway Crude Holdings LLC, which in turn is equally owned by Enterprise Seaway L.P., an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Enterprise Products Partners L.P. (&amp;quot;EPD&amp;quot;), and a wholly owned subsidiary of Enbridge, Inc. (&amp;quot;Enbridge&amp;quot;). Enterprise Crude Pipeline LLC (&amp;quot;ECPL&amp;quot;) serves as operator of Seaway. As operator, ECPL provides operating, administrative, marketing, construction, and other services related to the business and affairs of Seaway.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Seaway's assets include a 1,253-mile pipeline system, comprised primarily of two approximately 500-mile pipelines that provide north-to-south transportation of crude oil from the Cushing hub to the following locations: ECHO Terminal (Harris County), Texas; Seaway Freeport (Brazoria County), Texas; Nederland (Jefferson County), Texas; Enterprise Katy (Harris County), Texas and Phillips 66 Refinery Sweeny (Brazoria County), Texas.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Property, plant and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;The majority of revenues are derived from transportation of crude oil under intrastate and interstate tariffs. The tariffs specify the amounts to be paid by shippers for service between receipt and delivery locations and the general terms and conditions of transportation services on the pipeline system. In addition to transportation service, Seaway leases capacity on its pipeline system to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;an affiliate of Enbridge.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Seaway is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability to its members and, with the exception of the Texas Franchise Tax, if applicable, does not recognize this liability on the Company's financial statements. For purposes of calculating income taxes for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report), Seaway employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Seaway does not have any employees. All of Seaway's management, administrative and operating functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company (&amp;quot;Enterprise&amp;quot;) on behalf of ECPL. Seaway reimburses ECPL for the cost of Enterprise's employees who perform operating, management, and other administrative functions for Seaway under the terms of an operating agreement.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-369" contextRef="c-02">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;1) None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;2) None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;3) None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;4) None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;5) N/A&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
